  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Version 2.30.20 - AM030 converter null-handling guard recognition\n\n            Changed:\n            - Hardened AM030 converter null-handling detection so modern guard clauses `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(source)`, `ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrEmpty(source)`, and `ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace(source)` count as explicit null handling, including the named-argument shape `ThrowIfNull(paramName: ..., argument: source)`\n            - Guard calls whose `argument`/first positional argument is unrelated to the converter's source parameter (for example `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(context)`) still trigger AM030 so genuinely missing null handling keeps reporting\n\n            Validation:\n            - Full solution test suite passing on net10.0 with targeted AM030 and RuleCatalog coverage\n            - Rule catalog and sample diagnostics snapshot checks passing\n            - git diff --check clean\n\n            Previous Release: v2.30.19 - AM030 DI-injected converter false-positive suppression",
